# Physics-Based Telekinesis System Implementation Plan

## Overview
We'll create a telekinesis system that allows the player to:
1. Grab and manipulate physics objects
2. Create orbital effects with smaller objects around a grabbed large object
3. Rotate grabbed objects
4. Throw objects with damage based on velocity, momentum, and mass
5. Grab and drain health from enemies
6. Make enemies ragdoll when thrown and recover if health > 0
7. Implement AI awareness of telekinesis

## System Architecture

### 1. Core Components

#### A. Telekinesis Component (C++)
This will be the main component attached to the player character that handles telekinesis abilities:
```
- TelekinesisComponent (C++ class)
  - Grab/Release functionality
  - Object manipulation (movement, rotation)
  - Orbital system for smaller objects
  - Force calculation for throwing
  - Enemy health draining
  - Telekinesis targeting and raycast system
```

#### B. Physics Interface (C++)
An interface for physics objects that can be manipulated with telekinesis:
```
- ITelekinesisInteractable (C++ interface)
  - CanBeGrabbed()
  - OnGrabbed()
  - OnReleased()
  - GetMass()
  - ApplyTelekineticForce()
```

#### C. Health System (C++)
A component for managing health for both player and enemies:
```
- HealthComponent (C++ class)
  - Current/Max Health
  - TakeDamage()
  - HealDamage()
  - OnHealthDepleted()
  - DrainHealth()
```

#### D. Enemy AI Extensions
Extend the existing AI system to be aware of and react to telekinesis:
```
- New Blackboard keys:
  - IsBeingTelekineticallyManipulated
  - WasThrownByTelekinesis
  - LastTelekinesisAttackDirection
  - TelekinesisDetected
```

### 2. Implementation Phases

## Phase 1: Core Telekinesis Mechanics

### 1.1 Telekinesis Component Setup
- Create TelekinesisComponent C++ class
- Add to LianeCharacter
- Implement targeting system with line trace
- Setup input actions for grab/release/manipulate

### 1.2 Basic Object Grabbing
- Implement physics handle for grabbing objects
- Create telekinesis visual effect (material/particle system)
- Add hover effect for grabbed objects
- Implement object movement based on camera direction

### 1.3 Object Rotation
- Add rotation controls for grabbed objects
- Implement smooth rotation interpolation
- Create visual feedback for rotation mode

## Phase 2: Advanced Physics Interactions

### 2.1 Orbital System
- Detect smaller objects near grabbed large object
- Implement orbital physics calculations
- Create orbital path visualization
- Add force fields to attract/repel smaller objects

### 2.2 Throwing Mechanics
- Calculate throw force based on hold time
- Implement momentum and velocity tracking
- Add trajectory prediction visualization
- Create impact effects for thrown objects

### 2.3 Physics Damage System
- Calculate damage based on object mass, velocity, and momentum
- Implement impact detection system
- Create damage feedback effects
- Add object destruction for certain materials

## Phase 3: Enemy Interaction System

### 3.1 Health Component
- Create HealthComponent for player and enemies
- Implement damage and healing functions
- Add visual feedback for health changes
- Create death/incapacitation system

### 3.2 Enemy Telekinesis Interaction
- Make enemies grabbable with telekinesis
- Implement health drain mechanic
- Create visual effects for health transfer
- Add resistance mechanics for stronger enemies

### 3.3 Ragdoll System
- Implement ragdoll state for enemies
- Create transition between animation and ragdoll
- Add recovery system for enemies with health > 0
- Implement get-up animations

## Phase 4: AI Awareness and Reactions

### 4.1 AI Perception Extension
- Add telekinesis detection to AI perception
- Create new behavior tree tasks for telekinesis reactions
- Implement fear/flee responses to telekinesis
- Add group AI coordination against telekinesis

### 4.2 Advanced AI Behaviors
- Create defensive maneuvers against telekinesis
- Implement AI using cover to avoid telekinesis
- Add special enemy types resistant to telekinesis
- Create boss mechanics that counter telekinesis

## Technical Implementation Details

### 1. Physics Handling
- Use PhysicsHandle component for object manipulation
- Implement custom physics simulation for orbital objects
- Use physics constraints for controlled movement
- Apply impulse forces for throwing objects

### 2. Visual Feedback
- Create material parameter collections for telekinesis effects
- Implement particle systems for grab/throw/impact
- Add post-process effects for telekinesis vision mode
- Create dynamic sound effects based on object size/material

### 3. Performance Considerations
- Limit maximum number of orbital objects
- Implement LOD system for telekinesis effects
- Use physics sub-stepping for more accurate simulations
- Optimize raycasts with object filtering

### 4. Input System
- Primary action: Grab/Release (Left Mouse Button)
- Secondary action: Rotate Mode Toggle (Right Mouse Button)
- Tertiary action: Push/Pull (Mouse Wheel)
- Special action: Health Drain (E key when targeting enemy)

## Implementation Roadmap

1. **Core Mechanics (First Milestone)**
   - Basic object grabbing and movement
   - Simple throwing mechanics
   - Initial visual effects

2. **Advanced Physics (Second Milestone)**
   - Rotation controls
   - Orbital system
   - Physics-based damage

3. **Enemy Interaction (Third Milestone)**
   - Health system
   - Enemy grabbing
   - Health drain mechanics
   - Ragdoll system

4. **AI and Polish (Fourth Milestone)**
   - AI awareness and reactions
   - Advanced enemy types
   - Performance optimization
   - Final visual and audio polish

